  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1259 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nCore of mid to upper ridging will be quick to redevelop east over\nSE NM into W TX early this weekend, and then farther east over \ncentral TX late weekend through early next week. This will spell a\nwarming trend in high temperatures and drier weather with low \n(less than 10%) shower/storm chances confined to western higher \nterrain. While temperatures will not be as warm as earlier this \nweek, 100F-105F temperatures will expand near the Pecos River \nvalley, over the Upper Trans Pecos into Stockton Plateau, and \nnortheast Permian Basin, with higher elevations again rising back \ninto the 90F-95F range. Make sure to take proper heat safety \nprecautions (limit time spent outdoors during the hottest part of \nthe day, take frequent breaks in the shade if outdoors, drink \nplenty of water, and do not leave people or pets unattended in \nlocked vehicles). Lows will not warm as much even with more \nsoutherly near surface winds and LLJ repositioning farther east \nover the Stockton Plateau into Permian Basin. Early to middle of \nnext week, ridging develops northeast of the area, placing us in \nthe southern \"ring of fire\" with shower/storm chances increasing \nonce again and temperatures cooling very slightly. However, this \nfar out specifics remain murky, and no major cooling trend is in \nsight as we head into the month of September.",
